uman rights; critiques of the human rights movement; and the relationship of the\u00a0United States to the international system for the protection of human rights. The course will also explore issues such as the\u00a0death penalty, women's human rights, migration, climate change, global poverty, racism and xenophobia, and responses to mass atrocities. During in-class activities, students will have the opportunity to step into the shoes of a human rights advocate and work\u00a0with their classmates to address simulated human rights problems.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "LA", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2790, "crseId": 371567, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "LAW", "catalogNbr": "6043", "titleShort": "Int'l Hum Rights Theory & Prac", "titleLong": "International Human Rights in Theory and Practice", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1292, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "03:00PM", "timeEnd": "04:30PM", "startDt": "07/19/2021", "endDt": "07/31/2021", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "esa52", "firstName": "Elizabeth", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Anker"}], "pattern": "MTWRF", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "05/31/2021", "endDt": "08/21/2021", "addConsent": "D